From 55959ff4060f4d84e7bdbc4dcc764b60525d9280 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allcodernet <67543055+allcodernet@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 20:57:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 20/45] decide-schema: after, scoring/order_debias/temperature
 options, catalogue variants

Fields accept "after": 1 to 8 distinct names of other fields. compile
rejects with 400 invalid_schema and error.field = the dependent field:
not an array, an empty or too long array, a non-string entry, a
duplicate, an unknown name, the field itself, a cycle (reported at its
first field in declaration order, "after: cycle a -> b -> a") and a
dependency level above 8. field gains after, ancestors (indices of the
transitive closure, declaration order) and level; max_level gives the
deepest level.

options.scoring takes "tree" or "full_path", options.order_debias an
integer 0..8 (read as int64, so 2^32 + 2 does not wrap to 2) and
options.temperature a number in [0.05, 20] (0 in the struct = not
given), with the messages of spec 3.1.

render_catalogue(cs, variant, variants) lists each choice field's
options rotated left by floor(v * n / variants); (0, 1) gives the same
bytes as before (golden taken from the build before this change).
effective_variants gives K_eff = min(K, largest choice option count),
1 when K < 2 or without a choice field. The engine renders (cs, 0, 1).

handle_decide and handle_info return 500 engine "not implemented yet:
<feature>" for full_path, after, K_eff > 1 and temperature (first found,
in that order) until the engine implements them; request validation
errors still come first.
